#passage(("The next argument here is to do with the prophecies in the Hadith, and we've mentioned one in the beginning. And my argument goes as follows: Allahﷻ says in the Quran (AnNaml27:65): قُل لَّا يَعْلَمُ مَن فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ الْغَيْبَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ (Say: no one in the Heavens and the Earth knows the Unseen except Allah). So that means that the Unseen is specified for Allahﷻ; it's not for other people. He is the only one who knows the Unseen. Allah mentions the only exception is the Messengers, by saying (AlJinn72:26): عَالِمُ الْغَيْبِ فَلَا يُظْهِرُ عَلَىٰ غَيْبِهِ أَحَدًا (The knower of the Unseen, He does not tell the Unseen to anyone) إِلَّا (except) مَنِ ارْتَضَىٰ مِن رَّسُولٍ (what He pleases from a Messenger). So a Messenger, Allah can tell him some of the Unseen, can let him have some knowledge of the Unseen, like the Prophetﷺ when he told us all of these events that will happen in the future, that were of the Unseen for the Prophetﷺ and his generation; he told us in the future these things will happen. Only a Messenger can know the Unseen.", "And now when we look at the Hadith today, we find tens of examples of information about the Unseen. And if you are a Hadith rejector who pretends that the Hadith has no Revelation in it, then you have to explain to us: where did those authors of those books of Hadith, over thousand years before us, where did they get this information that these things will be happening today in front of our eyes? And we mentioned many examples of things that will happen: the Prophetﷺ talking about the Bedouin Arabs competing in building the tallest buildings, how the Prophetﷺ named the countries that will become Muslim, how the Prophetﷺ spoke about usury and interest and how they will be widespread, how he spoke about the Roman and Persian Empire, all of these different examples of the Unseen that are mentioned in the Hadith, which we use as evidence that Islam is the Truth, that the Prophetﷺ is a Messenger of God. You, as a Hadith rejector: based on the Quran, no one can know the Unseen except a Messenger of God. So if this Hadith is not coming from the Prophet, how did the authors know the Unseen? You've got no option except to disbelieve in the Quran, by saying the other people can know the Unseen, or to admit and accept the fact that this information, reliably and historically, traces back to the Prophetﷺ.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Complete Annihilation Of Hadith Rejector's Methodology! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Gc0mbEqasg", ((1654, "27:34–28:22"), (1702, "28:22–29:25"),), id: 2010)
