#passage(("We learn from the Prophetﷺ; that is why we have what we call the Sunnah or the Hadith, his life, to show us how to implement the teachings of the Quran. So it's no longer my understanding, or \"this verse means this according to me\". We say: \"Did the Prophet do it? Did the Prophet explain it that way? Did his Companions who he taught, did they practise it that way?\" If the answer is \"No\", then you are misrepresenting our teachings; you are misrepresenting the Quran. That's why Islam doesn't have this problem, because the Quran says go back to the Prophet, go back to his Companions, and implement the way he was implementing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Dismantles French Nationalism And Racist Ideologies! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CTdeXBAESWc", ((1898, "31:38–32:06"),), id: 2015)
