#passage(("The Quran is explicit and detailed in everything it teaches. Let's agree on that. I'm going to shake hands with that, 100%; I completely agree with that. Doesn't that same Quran tell you to go to the example of the Prophet? (alAhzab33:21): that the Prophetﷺ is our best example. Where's his example? It's not in the Quran. It's in the Hadith! Doesn't the same Quran tell you that the Prophet (alBaqarah2:151) is going to teach us the Quran and the Hikmah, which is the Hadith? Doesn't the Quran say that Allah sent down the Dhikr (anNahl16:44), the reminder, Revelation, referring to the Hadith, to explain the Quran to us? So the Quran is explicitly clear when it told you that the Prophet is going to explain the Quran to you. And the Companions' example: if you follow the Companions' example, like chapter:9 of the Quran (atTawbah), verse:100, then Allah will be pleased with you! But you're just taking a verse and ignoring the other verses.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Atheist Disproves The Quran?! Is Ezra The Son Of God? Islam Predates Judaism|”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0_RrmYKq0qU", ((1061, "17:41–18:32"),), id: 2017)
