// U ML415:42-68 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("Also, we have what is called the Hadith, which is the statements of the Prophet, the traditions of the Prophet. Other religions have that problem of \"your interpretation of the Quran verses\", \"my interpretation of the Quran\": each person's interpretation. When I speak to Christians, everyone has his own idea of Christianity. But what Muslims have is something else: we have that the Prophet is the one who tells us how to understand the Quran. We have his life, which is the Hadith, hundreds of thousands of Narrations of people describing how the Prophet lived his life, and how he practised the Quran. We can know how to practise the Quran. For us, it's the Prophet and his Companions: how they followed the Quran is how we should follow the Quran. So no one can come and say \"I understand it this way\". We say: \"Did the Prophet do this?\", \"Did the Companions do this?\" They say \"No\", we say: \"OK, then we don't accept it!\" Your interpretation is irrelevant to us, because what the Prophet did is what's important.", "You might have certain interpretations and things which are recent, like, for example, TV, things that didn't exist in the past. So the scholars use the Scripture to come into a ruling regarding these things: \"Should we deal with them?\", \"Should we not deal with them?\" But the main foundations, you have to go back to the Prophet, you have to go back to the Companions. You cannot bring your own interpretation and what you think is true and bring it into the Scripture. And that's what makes it unique!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “English Student Becomes Muslim! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vXu958o-hns", ((148, "2:28–3:17"), (203, "3:23–3:55"),), id: 2021)
// U ML294:511-578 | The Muslim Lantern | 4
#passage(("Now, the second logical problem with those Hadith rejecters is the idea of: who should we follow? I cannot name the amount of different Hadith rejecters I met, and all of them have their own understanding! And some of these understandings, I was shocked from how funny these understandings are! And this is not a claim I'm making; that's a fact. If you go online and you just research online for those Hadith rejecters, watch their videos: each and every single one of them believes that he's a Prophet who knows how to understand Islam. He doesn't say \"I'm a Prophet\", but he believes it, because he's legislating, and he thinks that his way is the right way of understanding the Quran! You go to the other one; he has a complete different understanding of the Quran. You go to a third one; complete different understanding of the Quran. And all of them have the same methodology, which is rejecting the Hadith.", "So who should we follow? According to you guys, who should explain to us these general verses that we already mentioned in the Quran? Which sect should we follow? Which Hadith rejector is your next Messiah you're going to follow and imitate what they say to you? Because you have to: you said there's guidance, and Allah has guided us. So where can we find in the Quran a direction to which Hadith rejector, which one of you, should we take? And if you say: \"No, you look at the Quran yourself and you come to the understanding..\", that will result in hundreds of millions of other people, who don't understand the Arabic language, like many of the Hadith rejectors, who are just making up their own understanding, and then everyone will go his own way. And that is completely wrong, and it does not make any sense.", "And do not forget the Quran is an evidence against you there. Why is it evidence against you? Because the Quran says that we should follow the Majority, the group of the believers. Allah says in the Quran (AnNisa4:115): وَمَن يُشَاقِقِ الرَّسُولَ مِن بَعْدِ مَا تَبَيَّنَ لَهُ الْهُدَىٰ وَيَتَّبِعْ غَيْرَ سَبِيلِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ نُوَلِّهِ مَا تَوَلَّىٰ وَنُصْلِهِ جَهَنَّمَ ۖ وَسَاءَتْ مَصِيرًا (That whoever opposes the Messenger..), like all of you, you are the opposers of the Messenger who reject the speech of the Messenger, (and goes any direction other than the way of the believers..). So the believers as a group, according to the Quran, have a way. And if you oppose the Messenger and go in any way other than the way of the believers, the Majority of the Muslims, نُوَلِّهِ مَا تَوَلَّىٰ وَنُصْلِهِ جَهَنَّمَ (then that person Allahﷻ is going to punish and send to the Hellfire). So that means the group of the believers, the جماعة of the believers, the whole of the believers, have a way, and you cannot be making your own way. And you all already admit and agree and know that you are a Minority. You are a fringe minority, not even 1% of Muslims. And the Quran tells us to follow the majority. How can we not follow majority when this verse is telling us to follow the majority! It's telling us that the group of the believers, if they agree on something (not the things that they disagree upon), but if they agree on something, then those believers you have to follow and tread the same path that they follow. So you explain to us who should we follow? And do not deviate from this question and say that the majority are misguided or this or that. Because the Quran is supposed to be guidance for us.", "There is a huge problem with those Hadith rejectors; this problem is to do with language. The Hadith rejectors play games and pretend that there is no such thing as the Arabic language that has been established, that the common folk of the Arab people, they understand what the Arabic language is. So whenever a verse opposes their understanding, they completely reject it and say: \"Oh, that's an incorrect meaning..\" But it is a meaning; we say this in classical dictionaries. They say: \"Oh, don't rely on the poets, rely on the Quran. The Quran is the way where you get your knowledge..\" The question is: who defines the words in the Quran? Where do you get your sources of language? We want to show your logical inconsistency, because many of the meanings that they give are based on these dictionaries and how the language is understood among the common people. But whenever a verse opposes their way and their understanding, they pretend as if language does not matter anymore: \"Oh no, we follow the Quran, not the language\", \"Don't follow the poets\", \"don't follow the books of dictionaries\", \"don't follow this and that; follow the Quran..\" Which dictionaries do you use? Whose understanding of the Arabic language do you use?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Complete Annihilation Of Hadith Rejector's Methodology! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Gc0mbEqasg", ((2039, "33:59–34:38"), (2078, "34:38–35:19"), (2125, "35:25–36:47"), (2211, "36:51–38:02"),), id: 2022)
// R quran_004_115.json
#refbox("Reference text: Quran 4:115, quran.com (Saheeh International)", (("4:115", "And whoever opposes the Messenger after guidance has become clear to him and follows other than the way of the believers - We will give him what he has taken and drive him into Hell, and evil it is as a destination."),))
