#passage(("When we look at the Quran and common sense, we have to accept that the Hadith is a necessity for you as a Muslim to follow Islam correctly. We know for a fact that there are different recitations of the Quran that are being read in the Muslim world today. For example, saying (AlFatiha:1) مَٰلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ / مَلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ and saying (AlHujurat49:6): فَتَثَبَّتُوٓاْ / فَتَبَيَّنُوٓاْ. All of these are different قراءات (recitations) that Muslims are reciting today. If you go to Morocco or if you go to Algeria, you go to Mauritania, you will hear the people reciting مَلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ. If you go to other parts of the world you'll hear them reciting مَٰلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ.", "And there's no issues for us as people who accept the Hadith, because we know that the Prophetﷺ said in the Hadith that the Quran has been revealed in seven أحرف, in seven different dialects, and you can recite the Quran in multiple different ways, so it's not one way of how you recite the Quran. So for us we've got no issues that there are different recitations of Quran. That does not attack the Quran in any way, shape, or form.", "But for you as a Hadith rejecter, you've got to tell us which one is correct. Is it مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ or is it مَلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ? And do you believe the Quran has been changed? Because if you say it's مَٰلِكِ يَوْمِ الدِّينِ, it's not مَلِكِ يَوۡمِ ٱلدِّينِ, then you're affirming that the Quran has been changed, and that opposes the Quran, chapter:15 (AlHijr15:9), where Allahﷻ says that He revealed the Quran and He's going to preserve it. So if Allah said He's going to preserve it, it must be preserved. And if it is preserved, then people cannot be reading it in different ways, millions of people around the world, because that will mean it is not preserved literally, because there's many people who read it and think it's the Quran.", "So if you say مَلِكِ is the only right way or مَٰلِكِ is the only right way, then you've admitted that the Quran has been changed, because the other word is not going to be the words of Allah, it's going to be the words of human beings. And if you say that both of them are correct, then show us where does the Quran mention that Allah revealed the Quran in different dialects and different ways of recitation? You need to show us where does the Quran say that explicitly, not your own twist and games. So if you cannot find us that in the Quran, then you have to accept that by no doubt it is in the Hadith. And the Hadith is the evidence and the Hadith is Revelation from Allahﷻ, and it explains this phenomena that Muslims have accepted for 1400 years, that there is Revelation other than the Quran, and that Allahﷻ revealed the Quran in different dialects and different أحرف.", "The Hadith rejecters say that we reject Hadith because men are fallible and they can make mistakes, and we don't trust that they completely transmitted this information correctly. We will ask them this simple question: Who transmitted to you the Quran? If you claim that the Hadith is corrupted because men are fallible and they make mistakes, we will say also you have to use the same argument for the Quran! Because the people who gave you the Hadith are the same people who gave you the Quran. Last time I checked, no Hadith rejector was living 1400years ago and none of them met Prophetﷺ and took the Quran from his hand. Rather they took it directly from their surroundings, from the Quran that is being printed around them, which traces back to the same people, same individuals, same Companions, same Narrators that narrate the Hadith. There's no difference between the Narrators of the Quran and the Narrators of the Hadith.", "You'll get some Hadith rejecters who say the Quran says that Allah is going to preserve it, that's why we believe it's preserved. But the problem with that is you cannot use the Quran without establishing first it's preserved! We can argue that this verse, that says the Quran is going to be preserved, is itself corrupted, someone added it later on, it's not from Allah. So you have to first establish that the Quran is not corrupted and then next we say: \"We understand this verse that Allah said it, now we accept that it's preserved.\" You need to establish first how it is preserved and how it was passed down to you. So we would like those Hadith rejectors to give us a rational reason of how did they get the Quran. And isn't it the same Companions, the same fallible men, that passed down the Hadith? So this is a clear logical inconsistency and picking and choosing what you want to follow, because you do not want to follow the Hadith, not because you are a Truth seeker.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Complete Annihilation Of Hadith Rejector's Methodology! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Gc0mbEqasg", ((1771, "29:31–30:08"), (1813, "30:13–30:30"), (1836, "30:36–31:00"), (1865, "31:05–31:58"), (1936, "32:16–33:01"), (1984, "33:04–33:55"),), id: 2028)
