#passage(("One thing which is very important is that those Hadith rejectors, they pretend and claim that they follow the Quran, but in the same time, you'll see them opposing the Quran in clear-cut things. For example, the idea of testimony, because the Hadith is a testimony of people. So when they claim that men make mistakes, why did Allah rely on those men's testimony as a valid source of information in many of the verses? For example, Allah says in some of the verses (AlBaqara2:282) وَاسْتَشْهِدُوا شَهِيدَيْنِ مِن رِّجَالِكُمْ ۖ (And get two witnesses from your men). So those men will testify and their testimony is a valid source of information, because there will be حدود (hudud: punishments) based on these testimonies. There will be money that is lost there, there will be things that are important. So, Allah says that this testimony is a valid source of information.", "Also Allah says (AlHujurat49:6) إِن جَاءَكُمْ فَاسِقٌ بِنَبَإٍ فَتَبَيَّنُوا (if someone who is disobedient comes to you with news then research that news), which means that if he's not a disobedient person, we can rely on his testimony and accept what he says as a reliable thing. If the Hadith is coming from people who are reliable, and they've given us a testimony, then that is based on the Quran, because the Quran accepts testimony, clearly, and Allahﷻ accepts testimony. So, if you pretend to follow the Quran, if you say that we cannot take people's testimony, and people are fallible and they make mistakes, then how can Allah rely on fallible people when it comes to punishments and people's money and wealth and all of that, and information that is being delivered to Muslims?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Complete Annihilation Of Hadith Rejector's Methodology! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Gc0mbEqasg", ((2286, "38:06–38:43"), (2323, "38:43–39:16"),), id: 2029)
