#passage(("We have a method. We have a whole science. It's called the Science of Hadith. Thousands of books are written on that Science, in which you have a Chain of Narration, individuals narrating from one another going back all the way to the Prophet. We need to know every single individual in the Chain. We need to know their reliability. We need to know their life, what their community said about them, their memory, whether it was strong or not. Did it become stronger or weaker when they became older? You know every information about them, sometimes what they used to eat for food!", "So if you were born in the 1700s and I said I heard from you, then that Hadith we would reject, because there's 200 years gap between me and you; it's impossible for me to listen and to hear the information from you, which means there is people in the Chain that are not there, which means now we cannot rely on the information that you're giving, because we do not know who's there that you learned from: that could be liars, could be people who are not reliable.", "So whatever the Prophetﷺ said, you had the people around him writing these Hadiths and transmitting those Hadith. And then you had Authors who wrote down these Ahadith and books, like Bukhari and Muslim, Abu Dawood, [an-Nasa'i] and all of these books. So they are written; no one today can come and write their own Ahadith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Visitor Questions Muslim On Hadith! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aVaXUL-Us6s", ((154, "2:34–2:54"), (185, "3:05–3:21"), (219, "3:39–3:52"),), id: 2056)
// U ML179:365-455 | The Muslim Lantern | 3
#passage(("Ahadeeth (Hadiths) is what is authentically narrated from the Prophet. Because he's the example for mankind, so it's important for us to know, of course, the mannerisms, the behaviors that he did, so we can imitate them and do the same things when it comes to mannerisms and acts and these specific things. Every single narration we take from the Prophet, even if that narration was \"do this\" only (it's two words), for these two words we need the chain of narration of reliable individuals.", "It's written and orally as well. So we even have written narrations of hadith very early, 100–200 years after the Prophet. We have [Malik ibn Anas]: his book alMuwatta, we have it, and he was in the 2nd century, in the first 200 years. You have Bukhari's writings. We have Muslim's. We have very early narrations, not only oral; but yes, we also mainly rely on the oral, because we have all of the information about the oral narrators written and attested to as well.", "There's no one in human history that goes to this extent when it comes to history, the reliability of information. No religion, no civilisation, nothing, nobody! Only Muslims went to that extent to preserve their tradition and make sure that whatever is passed down is reliable information, because we believe Prophet Muhammad is the last Messenger, and after him, until the Day of Judgement, there's no other Messengers. So the Message needs to be preserved, because people, you and myself, we need to know what the Creator wants from us, or requires from us.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Curious Canadian Grills Muslim With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XhEel3w9jYY", ((1278, "21:18–22:44"), (1490, "24:50–25:18"), (1526, "25:26–25:54"),), id: 2057)
// U ML025:773-814 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("We have the system. It proves that our system works, because we're rejecting more than we were accepting. That means there is a methodology that is being applied, which we're using to reject the hadith. And when you bring me a certain hadith that you may have an issue with, in the end you realize there's another answer. Perhaps you haven't been asking the person. There's an interpretation that perhaps you haven't seen. If it's authentic, there will be an explanation. However, because you haven't asked the right person, perhaps you may think, okay, this hadith now I need to discover, but that doesn't mean that therefore the hadith have issues.", "The Quran mentions the existence of another revelation other than itself; there is this rigorous process that we have in Islamic history for the authentication. So long as you agree with that, you agree with the principle, with the foundation.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Inquisitive Agnostic Grills Muslim On Cousin Marriage And Racism In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fvVrT_WHQxg", ((2639, "43:59–44:39"), (2696, "44:56–45:08"),), id: 2058)
