#passage(("Hamza Yusuf is actually referring to the concept of proving a negative. Now, yes, he's arguing that you can never prove that the Prophet never said something; however, there is no conflict between [that] and the idea that there's insufficient evidence for the attribution to the Prophet, peace be upon him. The grading of hadiths has been going on for centuries. I'm not bound to the gradings [of al-Albani]. I'm actually a qualified student of hadith that has the ability to judge hadiths for himself.",), "Farid Responds, “Christian Prince Responded to Me... BIG MISTAKE!!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0BJ-F_mukK8", ((894, "14:54–17:23"),), id: 2061)
