#passage(("For example, al-Razi says in أساس التقديس (The Foundation of Declaring Allah's Transcendence) that the intellect precedes the text, and if any text comes to us that the intellect does not accept, then we reject that text. This is an example. Another example: al-Razi says in his Tafsir (Exegesis), he rejects the clear cut hadith in Bukhari that mentions Ibrahim عليه السلام lied three times. He rejects the hadith that is narrated by four or five companions. I didn't say متواتر; I said four or five companions.", "A مشهور hadith (famous hadith), which is narrated by 3 individuals, is from the آحاد hadith. A عزيز: rare yet strong, any hadith conveyed by two narrators at every point in its chain of narrators. 3 is a مشهور hadith, and 4 is considered مشهور as well.", "The scholars disagree on what is a متواتر hadith. Some people say it has to be 10 chains or more individually in every level of the chain. By the way, scholars of أصول don't agree on what is متواتر hadith to begin with. But they say it is 10 narrators, for example (that's a number that some scholars say): 10 narrators, and they have to be 10 on every level of the chain.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Aggressive Ashari Interrogates Muhammed Ali On Stream!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k7SGfzzryjY", ((180, "3:00–3:22"), (278, "4:38–4:49"), (299, "4:59–5:18"),), id: 2063)
