#passage(("I do believe, by the way, this is not really a weird controversial thing; it's not something that's going to shake the core of our understanding of Christianity. We do believe that Christians saw Jesus die on the cross; we do believe they saw that. And it's not mass transmitted; it's transmitted through four anonymous sources. If I said to you I saw a zombie apocalypse right outside my house, and my whole town saw it, I'm the only person reporting it: it doesn't make it [mutawatir].",), "Farid Responds, “I Debated the Top Shia Clubhouse Debater! [Highlights]”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JKT_QIphTLI", ((494, "8:14–9:24"),), id: 2065)
// U FR174:1643-1835 | Farid Responds | 1
#passage(("By definition, the term mass transmitted can't be referring to two people. If you go back to Arabic works, the term [mutawatir] says that the number has to be so large that it's impossible for the people to have come together to fabricate a lie. Can two people physically come together and agree upon a lie? Obviously, it happens all the time. If that is the case, then how can two be enough for a hadith?",), "Farid Responds, “Full Debate: Farid (Sunni) vs Bayat (Shia)”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Iwc31dHLfco", ((4421, "1:13:41–1:14:23"),), id: 2066)
// U FR027:593-617 | Farid Responds | 2
#passage(("You said that we need two witnesses for our reports when it comes to witnessing financial transactions. But don't forget that it was only one prophet that was sent to teach that specific people. And when the prophet, peace be upon him, sent someone to Yemen, he sent [Mu'adh] with specific instructions. So there are cases where there's one person teaching, even when someone comes from a different land to learn from. It was never seen as you need to have two people to narrate something [for] it to be binding upon you. If you were in that society, would you say, I need someone else to verify, this is insufficient, I need three more women to narrate because I can't really trust you? You wouldn't say that.", "So this dismissing [ahad] despite having so many eyewitnesses, now this is too much. And this, by the way, goes beyond the level that's acceptable according to European historians and Greek historians and Roman historians: they never said you need 10 people narrating a report, or four people narrating a report.",), "Farid Responds, “Debate: Farid vs MuhammadFromGod - Reliability of Hadith System”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q3H7g7bsz3M", ((2776, "46:16–47:08"), (2868, "47:48–48:10"),), id: 2067)
