#passage(("If someone comes to you, he says to you there is a fire upstairs, let's say it's in the 10th floor, and you are in the first floor; you've not seen it, you've not seen smoke or anything, but they say to you there's a fire inside a specific flat. And then a second person comes that doesn't know the other person at all, and he says the same exact thing, and the third, fourth, fifth, sixth, seven, eight, nine, ten: they all come to you saying to you the same thing. Would you believe that there is a fire upstairs? So the Hadith is the equivalent, but the difference is that you know that every single person coming to you with the news is a trustworthy honest person too. Not just that there were people telling you news, but you know that they’re trustworthy and honest.", "Not only that, also there are written Ahadith. Imam Malik, we have his writings today; he died in the second century of Islam. He is very early, and we have his book Al Muwatta. There were two people between him and the prophet. He's very close to the time of the prophet.", "This person, Al-Bukhari, when he finishes the collection, he went to the people specialised in the Science of Hadith, the Science of Men (عِلْمُ الرِّجال ʿilm ar-rijal); they used to know the men, the liars and the authentic people and all of that. He went to them and he consulted with them and the whole Community to make sure: do you agree with this Ahadith to be authentic, or is there any mistakes? And then the whole Community accepted that book to be an authentic or most authentic book of Narrations, and since that time Muslims are using it, and that was very close to the prophet Muhammad.", "How do you know that Julius Caesar existed? How do you know Alexander the Great existed? None of those people have anything similar to what the Hadith has, noway near even. If you reject the criteria of Hadith, you have to reject all history, because nothing even comes close to that. So if I'm going to be skeptical to that extent, I cannot believe in anything!", "Muslims have the highest historical standard for their work. There's a testimony even of academics, or not Muslims; they would say the same thing to you: no one have anything similar to what Muslims have, preserving their history. Why? Because those people believe this is the word of God, so that we need to be sure that we're transmitting this. One narration of the Prophet is transmitted by over 50 Companions, and those 50 Companions have hundreds of people transmitting from them. This narration is: the prophet, he said: فمن كذب عليَّ مُتعمِّدًا، فلْيتبوَّأْ مقعدَه من النَّارِ (Who lies upon me intentionally, let him prepare his seat in the Hellfire). This narration is so mass transmitted because people took this seriously.", "So I don't have even a single doubt in my heart that this is authentic, because it's impossible. I have to believe there is a mass conspiracy, not only in one Community, but all of the communities of the people who wrote different books independently reporting the same information, and all of the men and all of those chains. So, I have to do that in order for me to reject the Hadith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Lady Questions Muslim On Hadith Reliability! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dWwbHO5Owpc", ((511, "8:31–9:17"), (560, "9:20–9:59"), (650, "10:50–11:14"), (723, "12:03–12:27"), (757, "12:37–13:09"), (821, "13:41–13:56"),), id: 2074)

=== 34.4 Corroboration of chains and the fabrication claim
// NODE P06.C02.S04
#author("Farid Responds")
