#passage(("The second argument is: all Sunnis and Quran only believe the Quran is preserved. Now, despite this, we all know that some people, when reciting the Quran, they make mistakes. You go to the mosque, you pray behind the imam, he makes a mistake sometimes. When you look into manuscripts, sometimes you'll find a mistake. Does this mean that the Quran is not preserved? Of course not. Despite that, no one is saying the Quran is not preserved. Having the Quran preserved does not mean that Allah will twist their tongues, preventing them from making a mistake, or will send a spirit to prevent a scribe from writing a mistake. We have access to [what the Prophet] recited; that in itself is the preservation of the Quran. You making a mistake yourself, that doesn't mean the Quran is not preserved. And this of course includes from the beginning of the Quran to the end of the Quran.", "But now let's compare this to hadith. Just because a fake hadith exists doesn't mean that we reject the authenticity of all hadiths. If a narrator made a mistake once upon a time, it doesn't mean that we reject all hadiths. If a reciter makes a mistake once upon a time, it doesn't mean that we reject all the recitations of the Quran. So you have to be consistent. Just because some fabrications exist in hadith, we can't dismiss all hadith. Just because there is a hadith that contradicts another, that doesn't mean we dismiss all the hadith. Similarly, because there is a recitation that contradicts another recitation, we reject one and we accept one. We don't reject all Quranic recitations and all Quranic verses, and we don't say the Quran is not preserved because someone made a mistake somewhere.", "So, why reject the hadith system? Why would someone say that it's invalid due to the existence of false hadith, while accepting the preservation of the Quran despite the existence of false recitations? If you're going to do it to hadith, you got to do it with the Quran. Why are you not doing it with the Quran?",), "Farid Responds, “Debate: Farid vs MuhammadFromGod - Reliability of Hadith System”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q3H7g7bsz3M", ((711, "11:51–13:25"), (805, "13:25–14:19"), (859, "14:19–14:45"),), id: 2086)
