#passage(("About slightly different wordings: we have something called “reporting The Hadith with the Ma'na”, رواية الحديث بالمعنى (narrating the narration with meaning). And this is permissible for anyone to do: to narrate a narration, to say The Prophetﷺ said X and then to give the meaning (does not have to be the exact wording of The Prophetﷺ), as long as certain conditions apply, which is that you understand the meaning, what The Prophetﷺ meant, number 1, and number 2, whatever words you use conveys the same meaning that The Prophetﷺ conveyed. And the Companions, they used to narrate certain Ahadith with the meaning, so they understood what The Prophetﷺ meant and they use slightly different words to give the exact same meaning. The wordings that you see in The Hadith, all of them are conveying the same meaning. If they are conveying more than one meaning, then they are separate Ahadith that The Prophetﷺ said them in different instances.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Coptic Christian Questions Muslim On Hadith! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5FilpKrRCFE", ((418, "6:58–7:45"),), id: 2087)
