#passage(("The idea of the historicity of Hadith is very important for Muslims. Understanding it will help you a lot as a Muslim, just to generally understand how Hadith grading works, and why do we accept certain Ahadith, why we don't accept certain Ahadith.", "The Hadith is history after all, so we want to compare this Hadith, which is history, to the Western history that many of those Hadith rejectors accept, or just normal history. They accept the history of their country, they accept the history of the Westerners, but when it comes to Hadith, they pretend that it does not work. So how does Western history, or non-Muslims, how do they actually view history? And how do they know if something is reliable or not?", "I'll give a basic example. What they do is that they find a letter, that letter is written down in the past, and it has a signature of a king of the time, and the information within that letter goes in line with the general information they have of the political atmosphere at the time. And they carbon date it to around the time that the king [lived]. So they say this letter is completely historically reliable; we don't have any issues, no skepticism towards it; we accept that as valid history.", "This is maybe the high standard of them accepting something to be reliable. Most of the history, there's a much weaker criteria for them to accept. For example, you hear about Socrates, Plato and Aristotle: Socrates said, Plato said. And none of this can be established that it is from them or it is from their time, or Alexander the Great did this or he didn't do that. So you find many of the people pretend this history is accurate and accept this history. They never question this history when someone tells them Aristotle said or Plato said, and they want to question Hadith, and they don't even understand how much scrutiny does it take for Muslims to say this specific Hadith is Authentic or this specific Hadith is Weak, which is a complete double standard and hypocrisy when it comes to looking at the historicity of something.", "So essentially, if you reject Hadith, you have to reject all history, Western history and non-Western history, because you're not going to find anything or anyone that goes into depth and so much scrutiny as Muslims do when it comes to the Hadith.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “A Complete Annihilation Of Hadith Rejector's Methodology! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1Gc0mbEqasg", ((2491, "41:31–41:44"), (2513, "41:53–42:14"), (2536, "42:16–42:52"), (2579, "42:59–43:39"), (2623, "43:43–43:54"),), id: 2103)
