#passage(("Allah says in the Quran, before creating Adam, chapter 2 of the Quran, he said to the angels, \"I'm going to place a [vicegerent] or representative on the earth.\" So Allah [willed] from the beginning, before Adam eating from the tree or being created, that he's going to place him on Earth. Adam is saying, \"How can you blame me for us going to Earth, while Allah already decreed that from the beginning, before I commit the sin?\" We did not come to Earth because Adam ate from the tree; this is what Adam is saying. The argument is about what Adam is saying: from the beginning Allah planned to take us down; it's not a consequence of the action. So that was the argument of Adam.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Finds Logical Problems With Islam?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CJuAdZhJIzo", ((1029, "17:09–17:52"),), id: 2120)
// U ML253:402-512 | The Muslim Lantern | 9
#passage(("There's a very popular narration, and I think it's misunderstood a lot. It says that there will be people who will come on the Day of Judgment with deeds the size of mountains. These deeds of these specific individuals will be made to disappear. So they will be doing good deeds, righteous deeds, actions, this and that. So why will all of these deeds disappear? They ask now the description of who these people are: there are people who are among the Muslims, and they pray in the night, and they do these specific things. When they're alone, they commit sins, they commit mistakes.", "Now he's talking about people who are from amongst this Ummah. When it comes to the Ummah, you have two types of the Ummah: the Ummah of Istijabah (Acceptance) and Ummah of the Da'wah (Invitation). Ummah can be everyone, literally, that the Prophetﷺ calls to Islam, the Muslim and the non-Muslim. But the Ummah of the Prophetﷺ means the people he was sent to, since his message started. And then you have the Ummah of Ijabah, the people who accepted the message. So this Hadith just says Ummah.", "And then it says these people do a lot of righteous deeds, good deeds, like the mountains. But Allahﷻ, He causes all of these good deeds to disappear on the Day of Judgment. Why? Why is mentioned in the Hadith: the reason is that they do specific sins in secret. Every time they are in seclusion or hidden in a hidden specific place that no one is around them, they are with Allahﷻ as the only One Who sees them, they break the commands of Allahﷻ.", "There's a few issues now. The first thing is that this Hadith first is disagreed upon its authenticity: there is a person in the Chain of Narration, he's an individual that there is a disagreement when it comes to his strength in narration. So there is a disagreement when it comes to the authenticity of this specific narration; that's the first thing.", "But let's say, assuming we take the authenticity of the narration, and we take the people who authenticated this narration. Now there's very problematic things to take. First, if you are alone, you do the sin in secret. The default position in Islam is that you're supposed to be doing the sins in secret. You're not supposed to be publicly doing them and sharing them with the people. Why? Because the Prophetﷺ said: every person of my Nation, he would be pardoned except those who expose and do their sins out there publicly for other people to see. Because when you do it publicly, then people see, and then it becomes normalized, and then other people are doing it, and then it becomes easier for people to do. So it's a lot more egregious for someone to be committing sins publicly. So it is absolutely better from an Islamic point of view that you keep the sins that you do between you and Allahﷻ. So do not listen to this narration and then get a misunderstanding for it, because this is not the case.", "In fact, in the Tafsir of the verse of the Quran (Alinshiqaq84:8), \"that he will be having an easy Hisab\", when Allahﷻ holds him accountable in the day of judgment for his deeds, there is a Hadith which is explaining that the person who hid the sins that he did, Allahﷻ says that you hid them and kept them in secret, so today I'll forgive them; no one else knows about them. You kept them hidden and secret, and then Allahﷻ forgives them for not exposing them. So as a Muslim, you shouldn't be exposing them.", "But in the same time, you shouldn't be thinking that it's OK now, when you're alone, you do things and you don't fear Allahﷻ. You should always keep in mind that Allahﷻ is watching, because Allahﷻ says in the Quran about the hypocrites (Annisa4:108): \"They hide from the people, they don't hide from Allahﷻ, and he's with them when they're at the night.\" So, as a Muslim, while you are hiding the shortcomings that you have, you shouldn't be thinking that it's OK, it's normal now, only Allahﷻ sees me, so I'm gonna do it. You should always have in mind that Allah sees you, and that should prevent you as much as possible from committing certain things, committing certain sins and certain bad acts.", "But this narration here is to be understood to be talking about the hypocrites. Yes, the hypocrites were among the Companions; they used to pray and they used to do all of these different things. But those are the people that Allahﷻ causes their deeds to go to waste. Allahﷻ says in the Quran (Alfurqan25:23): \"We came to the deeds they do and then we made them disappear.\" So this is referring to disbelievers. So this Hadith here is referring to the Munafiqeen, the Hypocrites, those who were doing major Nifaq. They were among the Companions; they were around them, claiming to be their brothers; they were praying and doing everything. But every time they go and they are in secret, they mock the religion, they mock Allahﷻ. Like Allahﷻ says in Surat (Albqara2:14), He says: \"If they see the believers, they say we believe,\" and then if they go now to their shayateen (Devils), their other disbelievers, they mock. They say, \"We are actually with you shayateen, we are only mocking the believers.\"", "So this Hadith is to be understood, if it's authentic, if you're going to take its authenticity: then, as a Muslim, you should understand this Hadith is referring to the Munafiqoon, the people who are hypocrites, major Nifaq, who show belief and then hide disbelief in their hearts. But the Muslims, their deeds are not just gone to waste fully like this, because as a Muslim, you're supposed to hide the shortcomings that you have.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Bible Hasn't Changed? Quranic Evolution? Can't Trust The Prophet? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-UhfvmM2IY8", ((1426, "23:46–25:29"), (1544, "25:44–26:05"), (1570, "26:10–26:45"), (1614, "26:54–27:13"), (1638, "27:18–28:13"), (1699, "28:19–28:50"), (1732, "28:52–29:26"), (1773, "29:33–30:34"), (1838, "30:38–31:01"),), id: 2121)
