#passage(("\"Allah will unalive you for not sinning\"! The Hadith has nothing to do with that. The Hadith is saying that (if human beings were beings created that do not sin), because Allah already have a Creation that doesn't disobey Him, which is the Angels, they already exist, and a Creation that always disobeys Allah, which is Satan. So these two Creations already exist. Now, Allah in this Narration is saying, (if we were not the creation that has the ability and capacity to sin and then seek forgiveness). Look at what the Narration is saying: (Seek forgiveness from Allah). So it talks about this close relationship with God. If we were not a creation that sins, has a capacity to sin, and then come back, and repent, and come closer to God, if we were not that creation, (Allah would replace us with a creation who would do that), because then that creation that doesn't sin already exists, and the creation that always sins already exists. We are a creation that is here to be tested. And for you to be tested for whether you will do right or wrong, you need to have the capacity to sin.", "So the Hadith here is not saying Allah will unalive you if you do not sin. The Hadith is talking about how sinning is a part of how God created us, because this life is a test, and we get closer to God through that. And if we were not like that, then we wouldn't be this creation, humans.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Proves Jesus Is God?! Sunnis Don't Pray Like The Prophet?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbnzQHBdTJo", ((668, "11:08–12:04"), (729, "12:09–12:26"),), id: 2122)
