#passage(("He says: the Prophetﷺ said, \"who innovates a Bid'ah in Islam\". That is a lie! The Hadith in Sahih Muslim which he's referring to does not say that. The Hadith in Sahih Muslim says: \"مَنْ سَنَّ سُنَّةً حَسَنَةً\". It doesn't say having Islam there. \"فَلَهُ أَجْرُهَا وَأَجْرُ مَنْ عَمِلَ بِهَا\". So, whoever does a Good Sunnah, he will have the reward of that Good Sunnah and the reward of everyone who does that good Sunnah. They misattribute things to people; they even mistranslate or mistransmit what the Prophetﷺ said. And the Prophetﷺ said, \"If you lie about me intentionally, prepare your seat in the Hellfire.\" It's not a small issue.", "What happened in this Hadith? There was a group of people that came to the Prophetﷺ. They were hungry; you could see the hunger in their faces. Then the Prophetﷺ, his face changed, and then he asked, \"Who wants to give charity to this group of people?\" Then one man stood up, a Sahabi, and he started donating, and he gave donations to the Prophetﷺ. Other people saw him, so they also stood up and started donating. So the Prophetﷺ said: \"Whoever does a good Sunnah,\" meaning initiating the action. He's initiating an action which is already a part of Islam, to give charity. So whoever initiates the act, he will have a reward for the act and everyone who followed him in the act. So he initiated giving the Sadaqa (Charity), so he gets the reward of the Sadaqa, and everyone who followed him gets the reward of the Sadaqa. Did that Sahabi in the Hadith bring a new tradition, a new way to worship, and then the Prophetﷺ said that this is a good Sunnah? And you call it \"innovation\". Is giving Sadaqa an innovation? Since when is giving Sadaqa an innovation? The people like this, they have to really twist everything about the religion. They have to twist things about the Deen of Allahﷻ in order for them to support their own cause or support what they want you to believe in.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Quran Scientific Claim Debunked? Bida'ah Is Good? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5z_gp4XDYzs", ((1371, "22:51–23:31"), (1424, "23:44–24:50"),), id: 2123)
