o are the reason for misguiding those people. So, they take those sins away. Why do they take the sins? Because they're the cause of the misguidance. And then the Muslim is released. He's free from the fire because he's forgiven by Allah, while the disbeliever who's the cause of misguidance is still put in hellfire because of him misguiding people.", "Everything is explained in the Quran. Everything is explained in the Hadith. That's why it's not a ransom. It's the sins that they have committed and led other people to misguidance. They are bearing these sins. Because I could do bad myself, and I bear that sin. But I could also lead others to do bad. I could entice others to do bad. And in Islam, when you do that, you bear the sin. Prophet told us, \"Person who initiates an evil deed, he will have the sin of that deed and everyone who does that deed.\" The prophet told us that the two children of Adam, the one who killed his brother, he's bearing the sin of killing of everyone who kills later on, because he initiated the first killing. So, in Islam, that is our position. You can't just misguide people and only bear your own responsibility. So, those Jews and Christians are going to bear the sins. It's their sins. But it's the other people who've done them, because they were misguided by them.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Christian Attempts To Trap A Muslim But This Happens! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R6rZ76lfXpk", ((759, "12:39–13:21"), (802, "13:22–16:30"), (993, "16:33–17:00"), (1022, "17:02–17:43"), (1065, "17:45–18:38"),), id: 2134)
