#passage(("Fixed term means, as the hadith explains, that the sun will end under the throne of [Allah], and then it will be told to go back, and then it will rise from the opposite side, which is a sign of the day of judgment.", "When you have a book and it brings narrations, nowhere would that person tell you that I'm only bringing authentic narrations. Many people in their books say in the beginning, in the introduction of their books, that they are bringing news. None of them have a criteria of only bringing you authentic narrations, which is why they put the chain of narration there: this person reported from that. Why do they put it? It's upon you now to do the investigation. They've done their work. They've given you the chain of narration. Now, through the science of hadith, you look at the people in the chain and you come to the conclusion, as a scholar of hadith, whether this is authentic or this is not authentic. Now there is a weak narration. We already know it's weak. It's certainly 100% weak, because it contradicts not only this narration, other narrations as well.", "There's no sunset. In reality, of course, it's a figurative term that we use in language. That's why people Google when is the sunset. But if now you're talking about the sun itself, the narration says the sun is moving.", "All of these things are metaphysical things, realities. So, [prostration]: Allah says in the Quran, and this is for everything, there is not anything in existence except that glorifies Allah; then Allah says, but you do not know how they glorify Allah. So how they prostrate, the howness of how they do it, of course it's not the same way we're doing it. So that's the first part, about prostrating in its own way, in the way Allah created it to worship Allah, following Allah's commands, systems, order, etc.", "The sun is moving right now. Do you know where the throne is according to Muslims? Not in the seventh heaven. Above everything. Let's hypothetically, for the sake of demonstration, give this example. You have seven layers of that which is above us, and call it universe. Everything we see is just the first layer. So we have the first layer. Then we have a second layer, third layer, fourth layer etc. Then you have the seventh layer. Then you have heaven and hell. You have all these things. Then you have the throne of Allah above everything. The sun is under the throne of Allah.", "How does it ask permission? It is following the system and the law of Allah. Rise in this hadith is referring to our perspective. Meaning it asks Allah's permission to follow the laws that Allah has given it to do. I don't see any contradiction.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Confronts Muslim On Mistakes Found In The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L-Zd3evV1oY", ((1594, "26:34–26:46"), (1662, "27:42–28:44"), (1768, "29:28–29:48"), (1810, "30:10–31:08"), (1876, "31:16–32:19"), (1959, "32:39–33:03"),), id: 2140)
