#passage(("I just want to share a hadith that I will never accept, even though it's been used as a miracle for Islam, or proof for Islam. The hadith goes something like this: Ibn Abbas is asking the prophet, peace be upon him, \"These settings of the sun, to where does it set? These risings of the sun, to where does it rise?\" And the prophet, peace be upon him, allegedly replies, \"It is calm; it doesn't leave, nor does it disappear.\" So he's suggesting that the sun is fixed. And then he says, \"It sets away from some people and rises for others\"; some people say it sets and other people say it rose. So it's implying that it's a matter of perception, since he says in the beginning of the report that the sun is calm and it doesn't leave, and secondly it's suggesting that it rises for some people and it sets for different people at different locations. So this hadith is used as proof for Islam.",), "Farid Responds, “I Refuse to Accept this Miracle for Islam!!”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nw9Tl8RwWLM", ((21, "0:21–1:47"),), id: 2146)

