#passage(("A quick summary of it is: you have some people that came to the prophet, peace be upon him, and they're accepting Islam, and they complain about some ailments that they have, and the prophet, peace be upon him, tells them to drink camel urine and camel milk. So they head off to an area, and they drink that camel urine and camel milk, and a while later they become better, and after they're better they kill the camel herder that was taking care of the camels, and they steal the camels, and they are caught and they are killed for doing those acts.", "Now keep in mind that these are pregnant camels, and the urine of pregnant mounts have healing properties. In any case, camel urine has [healing] properties, and all you got to do is head over to PubMed and type camel urine in the search box and go through some of the articles there. Science is on the side of Islam in this one.",), "Farid Responds, “The Camel Thieves and Camel Urine Story”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vD0K4p2lc8I", ((59, "0:59–1:39"), (99, "1:39–2:13"),), id: 2147)
