#passage(("If something is extracted from pregnant [mare] urine, then you better believe that the pure thing has those same benefits. Apus then deceives his audience, pretending to make it seem like the articles I shared only talk about components of camel urine and not the actual pure [camel] urine. This is false. The articles I'm presenting are not talking about extracts; they're talking about the pure camel urine. If there's nothing wrong with you, then you shouldn't drink camel urine. He's challenging me to drink camel urine to prove it's beneficial. Why would I do that when I don't have a disease that the [Uraniyyin] that came to the prophet, peace be upon him, had? Imagine I tell Apus to prove that chemotherapy is beneficial by taking chemotherapy even though he doesn't have cancer.",), "Farid Responds, “Apus Challenged me to drink Camel Urine”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RVVwo0yesxw", ((171, "2:51–4:36"),), id: 2152)
