#passage(("In medicine, you don't only use the excrements of animals, not only camels, but animals in general, but even insects to create antibiotics and medicine. That Hadith refers to a specific stomach disorder that they have, and you will find that camel urine is used in medication for that specific disease. Before you base a judgment, you could ask a question, and understand!", "I would rather talk about foundational things, because what you're doing right now is you're clutching to straws: things which you don't understand, and they're not the foundation of the religion. A Narration about a group of people, who the Prophet prescribed them to do a specific thing which was medicine for them, how does that got anything to do with the foundations of Islam, or the religion, or extremism?", "This only book that you have in your hand have over 6,000 Hadiths. You made a conclusion over everything else. And that's why I said: a person who's not a person of knowledge cannot pick Bukhari, and Muslim, and these books, and read them, because you collect these Narrations, and through collecting these Narrations, you understand the wider context, and you understand in reality why is this being said. But a person who doesn't want to learn, he doesn't ask a question, he makes a judgment. He says: this is ridiculous, and extremists will use this Narration about the camels. They don't use it; you're just creating something out of nothing.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Researcher Confronts Muslim On Extremist Teachings! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G5Mgp9SzUc0", ((2455, "40:55–41:28"), (2491, "41:31–41:53"), (2528, "42:08–43:06"),), id: 2153)

=== 35.7 The fly in the drink and other medical hadiths
