#passage(("Confusion in this report is similar to the confusion that would occur if a groom invited folks to his party and said that men that are invited need to be dressed in black. Your best friend, who happens to be the groom's brother, says: my brother said dress in black or dark clothes. Now, due to the way he says it, you think that black or dark clothes were the words of the groom, but in reality it was the brother that said that. And due to this you assume it's optional, black or dark clothes, and due to this you go to the wedding dressed up in a dark brown suit, and you happen to stand out.", "And this Hadith falls under the same issue. In this Hadith something similar happens, where the narrator reports on his confusion, and David has understood it to mean that the prophet peace be upon him said both things. Now, this is a more accurate translation according to David: \"had it licked\" means had it licked by someone else. However, this is an incorrect interpretation. The Hadith actually says: let him not wipe his hand until he has licked it, or let him not wipe his hand until he had it licked. In other words, the narrator of the Hadith wasn't certain, and hence he used both terms due to his uncertainty. This is a valid conclusion, because we have reports of the Prophet peace be upon him saying \"lick your fingers\" alone. We also have several reports of the Prophet peace be upon him and his companions licking their own fingers, and we don't have reports of them licking the fingers of one another, and thus David's conclusion was incorrect.", "Three issues with David using this report. Firstly, the Hadith comes through a weak narrator. Secondly, there is no tongue being mentioned; instead it says he placed his mouth onto his mouth. By the way, [al-Hasan] is the grandson of the Prophet peace be upon him, and not some random boy that he found off the street. It seems like David is arguing the prophet peace be upon him was a homosexual and into incest.", "The report seems to be disconnected between Abd and [Muawiya], since it doesn't seem like he had met the latter. Again, this report is not about some random little boy on the street; it's about Hassan, the grandson of the Prophet peace be upon him. The report isn't even clear if there was any tongue, since the report clearly says \"or lips\". And perhaps most importantly, the prophet didn't say this; rather it was the opinion of [Muawiya], if [Muawiya] indeed said such a thing. David, why do you keep saying boys in plural, when it's clearly one boy? Why do you have to make everything seem to be sexual? If someone did this to the Bible, you think that they wouldn't be able to turn stories in the Bible to something sexual? Like for example these verses about Prophet Elisha: couldn't someone interpret this to be something sexual?", "Two ways of looking at this particular narration. The first is that this is actually a mistake from one of the narrators of the Hadith. This is a Hadith by [Anas], while the report states that the prophet peace be upon Him used to pass by his wives without intercourse, meaning that he would visit them all in one night.", "But let's assume that the narration of [Anas] was correct, and that the prophet peace be upon him did indeed have intercourse with multiple women while only bathing once, referring to a fullbody bath. Bathing doesn't negate that the prophet peace be upon him was cleansing himself partially. So basically washing your genitals or washing your armpits wouldn't count; there's a difference. So if someone was to wash every single inch of his body except for his hair, that wouldn't count. David seems to be unaware that the prophet peace be upon Him cleansed himself whenever he had intercourse. He would say: when anyone amongst you has sexual intercourse with his wife and then he intends to repeat it, he should perform ablution. In other words, he would wash up partially even though he was going to have intercourse with the same wife, let alone a different wife.",), "Farid Responds, “David Wood Challenged Me to Refute This Video! (5 Disgusting \"Facts\")”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jWWGA_607MI", ((154, "2:34–3:23"), (203, "3:23–4:43"), (310, "5:10–5:53"), (378, "6:18–7:39"), (502, "8:22–8:41"), (527, "8:47–9:59"),), id: 2167)
