#passage(("I'm not simply going to be refuting David [Wood's] claim: drinking the prophet's blood takes you to paradise. But I'm also going to be exposing the deception involved.", "So what does he say? Woe to you from the people, and woe to the people from you. And that says: but he did not object to what he had done. But it just said that he did object! Saying \"woe to you from the people and woe to the people from you\" is an objection.", "I'd like to point out a couple of things here. Firstly, the hadith of [Abdullah ibn] Zubair: if we actually go back to the source David is providing us with right now, which is Islam Q&A, the page that David was going through, it says: \"Secondly, some of the Sahaba may Allah be pleased with them drank the blood of the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and in some reports it says that he approved, and in others it says that he denounced them.\" That's exactly my point: this hadith is a hadith in which the Prophet peace be upon him denounced [Abdullah]. It's quite clear: it was narrated from [Abdullah] may Allah be pleased with him that he came to the Prophet peace be upon him whilst he was being cupped, and when he has finished he said: take this blood and pour it away so no one will see it. He went and drank the blood. He said: what have you done? He said: I put it in the most sacred place where I thought it would be most hidden from the people. He said: perhaps you drank it? He said: yes. He said: why did you drink the blood? Woe to the people because of you, and woe to you because of the people.", "It doesn't include the part that David shared from [ash-Shifa] [of Qadi Iyad], which says that he did not rebuke him. We can clearly see that he is being rebuked here. It seems like David is just jumping around picking sources that fits him. He's aware of the existence of this article on this website.", "In regards to what David includes about the father of Abu [Sa'id], Malik, it says in the beginning: [Ibn Hajar] said in [al-Talkhis] concerning this topic there is a [mursal hadith]. Now what is a [mursal] hadith? A disconnected [hadith]. I think if he knew [what a mursal] hadith was, he wouldn't even quote this, because it's not proof for him.", "This is another important part that David left out, the conclusion: \"Out of the reports about the Sahaba drinking some of the blood of the Prophet peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the reports about [Abdullah] is the most sound, although there is debate about this; no other [report is sound].\" David, you can't use anything except for the one report that rebukes [Abdullah]. That's the only thing that you can use; even that isn't all that great.",), "Farid Responds, “The Deception of David Wood - Blood of the Prophet ﷺ”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LlobqAy56Nw", ((2, "0:02–0:11"), (91, "1:31–1:51"), (163, "2:43–4:14"), (257, "4:17–4:39"), (289, "4:49–5:31"), (331, "5:31–6:05"),), id: 2170)
