#passage(("We have an exact 100% similar situation, without the castration obviously, happening at the time of the Prophet Muhammadﷺ. There is a man of the A'rab – A'rab are the people who live in the outskirts of Mecca and Medina, very rigid people living in tents and stuff like that. So one of them came to the mosque. This is an actual incident that happened in the life of the Prophetﷺ; it's in our Narrations and Hadith, in the most authentic books. The man came to the Prophetﷺ, and the Muslims were there; he went to the mosque and he started urinating.", "The Companions see him and they're about to take a hold of him. Of course: how could you do this? They want to capture him. They want to take him. They want to remove him or push him or do whatever they want to do to him, because of course they believe this place is the house of God. But the Prophet of Allah tells the Companions: stop, do not stop him from urinating. He didn't just tell them to stop. He said: لا تُزرِموه, do not interrupt him while he's urinating. Let him finish. And when he finished urinating, then the Prophet told them: throw water on top of the urine, obviously to purify the area, basically cleanse it with water.", "Then the Prophet went to that man. The Prophetﷺ said to him that this is a house of God, this is a mosque, it's a place of worship; it's not appropriate for us to do something like this in a house of God, a place of worship. Imagine the mercy. Here's a Prophet of God telling us how to behave. Story doesn't end there, where the Prophet just tells him that and lets him go. Then the Prophet turns around and he speaks to the Sahaba, the Companions, and he said to them: we were sent from God -or God commanded us- مُيَسِّرين, as people who are lenient, people who are easy, people who are merciful; not مُعَسِّرين, not people who are of difficulty, not people who bring about hardship to other people.", "Many Muslims heard this story, because we know the character of the Prophetﷺ, not what people keep character assassinating the Prophetﷺ with: lies and fabricated stories and fairy tales. These are real life events. This is what Muslims are being taught, how to behave. So even if this story, fairy tale story, was true, all of these Muslims went against the action of the Prophetﷺ, when they have an actual precedent of how to behave, and they have a clear teaching of the Prophet that we are sent easy and lenient to the people!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Famous Hollywood Actor Terrence Howard Claims That Islam Is NOT Merciful | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h_iKYfrgraE", ((436, "7:16–7:54"), (479, "7:59–8:46"), (529, "8:49–9:49"), (596, "9:56–10:19"),), id: 2171)

