#passage(("Hadith At-turba التربة: “Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, created the earth on Saturday, and created the mountains...” This Hadith is one of the Ahadith that are well-known to be rejected by multiple, different Scholars. So there is one answer: that there are Scholars who rejected this Hadith due to the fact that it is clearly in opposition apparent of the Quranic text. And another way to answer: that there are Scholars who did explain this Hadith in another way: these are periods of time in which creation happened, and I believe Al-albani الألباني gave that kind of understanding to this Hadith. Either way, you can pick any understanding you like to this Hadith. You can completely say that there's weakness in this Hadith, because this is a well-known criticized Hadith, and this is not a secret in the Islamic community. This حديث التربة is a well-known, criticized Hadith. Our tradition is simple: we accept the Hadith based on the Chain of Narration. This Hadith has been criticized for both: for the متن and for the إسناد as well. Albukhari weakened the Hadith; Ali ibn al-Madini did, Yahya ibn Ma'in, Abd ar-Rahman bin Mahdi and other people weakened the Hadith.", "The book of Bukhari is a book of Hadith in which he collects narrations of the Prophetﷺ. How do we know whether Bukhari said something or not? We have got books, other books. For example, if Harb Alkirmani says Imam Ahmad said X, Y and Z, then we say Imam Ahmad said X, Y and Z. We don't go to the Musnad المسند of Imam Ahmad, because the Musnad is a book of Hadith. So we go to the other books that Imam Al-Bukhari has written, or books that have quotations, statements, the Imam bukhari made to his students. For example, one of the students of Imam Al-Bukhari asked him: what do you think about Hadith X, Y and Z? And then Imam AL-Bukhari said: \"I think the Hadith X, Y and Z is weak\", or \"I don't accept this Hadith X, Y and Z\". This is how criticism works in علم الرجال Science of Narrators (Biographical evaluation).",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Arab Christian Confronts Muslim On Bukhari! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eRixK0aX2eM", ((12, "0:12–1:03"), (83, "1:23–1:55"),), id: 2179)
