#passage(("The report that says the Quran and the Sunnah, that's a false report. The hadith that says hold on to the Quran, that's the hadith of [Jabir] that comes through the path of Muhammad from his father from [Jabir]: that is an authentic report that is in Muslim, and it only mentions holding on to the Quran.",), "Farid Responds, “Debate: Farid vs MuhammadFromGod - Reliability of Hadith System”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q3H7g7bsz3M", ((4951, "1:22:31–1:22:50"),), id: 2180)

=== 35.12 Lesser-known narrations of Anas and the Ansar
// NODE P06.C03.S12
#author("Farid Responds")
// U FR005:1-36 | Farid Responds | 3
#passage(("While going through Sahih al-Bukhari, I was thinking to myself, a lot of these reports are not narrations that are often quoted. Some of them are actually quite rare in terms of them being quoted on social media or in the masjid or whatever. We often hear the same narrations in the Bukhari and Muslim and whatever being brought forward again and again, whether they're controversial in nature or they're brought up in certain discussions that they're very relevant towards. However, there's a bunch of narrations that completely get overlooked. Some of these reports have this major theological lesson, and some of them are not really ideologically significant, but they're just enjoyable to share.", "Anas ibn Malik, when narrating this first report, is actually a kid. Anas reported that Allah's messenger, peace and blessings be upon him, had the best disposition amongst people. He sent me on an errand one day, and I said, \"By Allah, I would not go.\" I had, however, this idea in my mind that I would, as Allah's apostle, peace be upon him, had commanded me to do. I went out until I happened to come across children who had been playing in the street. In the meanwhile, Allah's messenger, peace be upon him, came there and caught me by the back of my neck from behind me. As I looked towards him, I found him smiling, and he said, \"O Anas, did you go where I commanded you to go?\" I said, \"Allah's messenger, yes, I'm going.\" Anas further said, \"I served him for 9 years, but I know not that he ever said to me about a thing which I had done, why I did that, or about a thing I had left as to why I had not done that.\"", "Anas reports, \"While leading you in prayer, I do not shorten anything in the prayer. I pray as I saw the messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, leading us.\" He, Thabit being the narrator, said, \"Anas used to do that which I do not see you doing. When he lifted his head from bowing, he stood up that one would say he has forgotten. And when he lifted his head from prostration, he stayed in that position till someone would say he has forgotten.\"",), "Farid Responds, “Test your Knowledge - Ten Hadiths”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LOCLrBxohGM", ((7, "0:07–1:22"), (109, "1:49–2:51"), (177, "2:57–3:26"),), id: 2181)
// U FR005:48-82 | Farid Responds | 6
#passage(("The Prophet, peace be upon him, said there is none amongst the Muslims who plants a tree or sows seeds and then a bird or a person or an animal eats from it, but it is regarded as a charitable gift for him. And by charitable gift here, it means that it counts for him as a reward.", "Anas ibn Malik used to pass by a group of boys and he'd greet them and said, \"The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to do so.\" Someone may be asking, \"What's the point of this? He's greeting children. How's this beneficial?\" Well, this tells you something about the nature of the Prophet, peace be upon him. Some people, especially disbelievers, they imagine that the Prophet, peace be upon him, was someone that was stern and harsh and cold. When reality, he was friendly with everyone. He was friendly with children. The Hadith in itself is proof of that.", "Anas narrated that the hair of the Prophet, peace be upon him, used to hang down up to his shoulders. There are multiple narrations that speak about the length of the hair of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and it's quite natural that some of them would display the Prophet's hair, peace be upon him, as being longer or shorter. However, from what I recall, this is the narration with the longest reported hair for the Prophet, peace be upon him.", "The Prophet said, \"Allah will say to that person [of] the hellfire who will receive the least punishment, if you had everything on the earth, would you give it as a ransom to free yourself?\" He will say, \"Yes.\" Then Allah will say, \"While you were in the backbone of Adam, I asked you much less than this, i.e. not to worship others besides me, but you insisted on worshipping others besides me.\"", "Anas reported Allah's messenger peace be upon him saying, \"The son of Adam grows old, but two desires in him remain young, desire for wealth and desire for life.\" Narrated Anas that the prophet peace be upon him said, \"None of you will have faith till he wishes for his Muslim brother what he likes for himself.\"", "Asim narrated, \"I said to Anas, 'Did Allah's apostle make Medina a sanctuary?'\" He replied, \"Yes, Medina is a sanctuary from such and such place to such and such place. It is forbidden to cut its trees and whoever innovates a heresy in it or commits a sin therein will incur the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people.\" Of course, this is referring to the sanctuary of Medina. However, it does also apply to the sanctuary of Mecca.",), "Farid Responds, “Test your Knowledge - Ten Hadiths”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LOCLrBxohGM", ((241, "4:01–4:17"), (259, "4:19–4:52"), (296, "4:56–5:22"), (324, "5:24–5:51"), (353, "5:53–6:13"), (377, "6:17–6:47"),), id: 2182)
// U FR013:1-36 | Farid Responds | 4
#passage(("Sometimes you find that Hadith rejectors or ex-Muslims, they say things like I rejected the Hadith after I read the Hadith. You telling me that Hadith rejectors actually sat down and read the Hadith properly, an actual book of Hadith? The vast majority of the Hadith are not problematic. In fact, a very large number of them have these indirect Iman boosting type of information. And a lot of it's just mundane information, slice of life information that just makes you appreciate their times.", "Here's something that you may have not come across. It's something I noticed by piecing narrations together. You can actually find this in Bukhari and Muslim, in which the prophet, peace be upon him, starts listing the clans of the Ansar and he says that the best of the Ansar are Banu Najjar and then Banu Abdul Ashhal and then Banu Harith bin Khazraj and then Banu Sa'idah. The narrator of the Hadith is Abu Usaid Sa'idi. He's from Banu Sa'idah. So, he mentions his clan, his subtribe, as fourth place out of the top four clans of the Ansar. And Abu Usaid as-Sa'idi says, \"You guys are going to accuse me? If I was someone that was going to lie about the prophet, peace be upon him, then I wouldn't mention us as number four.\"", "Banu Najjar, that includes Anas ibn Malik, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, Zayd ibn Thabit. It's one of the bigger, well-known clans of the Ansar. Banu Abd al-Ashhal, that's the tribe of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. It's also the tribe of Usayd ibn Hudayr, as well as of course his father, the famous Hudayr al-Kata'ib. And then you have Banu Sa'idah, which is the famous tribe that is known for Saqifah Bani Sa'idah, which is led by Sa'd ibn Ubadah, and in this report, Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi.", "What I find really interesting here is that Sa'd ibn Ubadah is actually very upset that his clan is mentioned as the fourth. He said, \"Prepare my donkey so that I could go to the prophet, peace be upon him,\" to speak to him about this. It's something that weighed down massively on him. And then he was spoken out of it. And he just gave up on the idea of speaking to the prophet, peace be upon him, on his ordering and favoring of the different clans of the Ansar.",), "Farid Responds, “I just noticed something about these hadiths...”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YXz5dQQbBVY", ((0, "0:00–0:46"), (52, "0:52–1:49"), (112, "1:52–2:31"), (151, "2:31–3:16"),), id: 2183)

