#passage(("The guy doesn't even know how to pronounce the name of one of the founders of the 4 schools of thought, Abu Hanifa. He says \"Abu Hanafi\"! So you can see this guy is 100% reading some sort of a script that someone wrote for him. Has even no clue who these people are.", "Then he says, Oh, [Ja'far as-Sadiq] came 70 years after the Prophet. So how did he get the knowledge from the Prophet then?! Who did he get the knowledge from, if he came 70 years after the Prophet? Did he see the Prophet in his dream and told him how to pray?", "Here is the LIE. He was trying to make this argument: \"Sunnis take their religion from the 4 Imams, and these people take it from Ja'far.\" No! That's not how it works. You're a liar and you know it, because we don't take from the 4 Imams and we stop there. We only take from the 4 Imams, because they took from people earlier than them. You go to Imam Ahmad and read his books. Read the \"Book of Sunnah\", read any of the Books of Imam Ahmad or read the Books of Malik like Muwatta Malik. What does it have? It all has Narrations: Malik heard from Nafi', heard from Ibn 'Umar, heard from... That's just how the Narration works. Malik hears from his teachers, and his teachers heard from their teachers. We don't just take from Malik and we don't just take from ashShafi'i. At Tirmidhi? We take from his Book! alBukhari and Muslim! They're not from the 4 Imams! So why are you lying? We take things from the Prophet. Those people were only people who transmitted what the people before them said, going all the way back to the Prophet. So obviously that's a lie, trying to pretend that Muslims only take from the 4 schools of thought. That is the strawman argument that he built his whole story about.", "And now he says: Ja'far asSadiq was teaching... Or let's say Abu Hanifa and Malik took some Narrations from him, or learned from Imam Ja'far. You don't understand what they learned from Ja'far asSadiq? Imam Malik had tens of teachers. Imam Ahmad had tens of teachers. Abu Hanifa had tens of teachers. What do we mean when we say they took from someone? They went and took Narrations from them. They told them, I heard from this person, hearing from this person, the Prophetﷺ said... That's what it means that Abu Hanifa took from Ja'far asSadiq or that Malik took from Ja'far asSadiq. It means that they took Narrations from them. It doesn't mean that they're the source of the knowledge, like you're trying to portray. So it's all strawman arguments and lies for people who are not familiar with Islamic history.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Proves Jesus Is God?! Sunnis Don't Pray Like The Prophet?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbnzQHBdTJo", ((1205, "20:05–20:22"), (1224, "20:24–20:35"), (1257, "20:57–22:03"), (1332, "22:12–22:57"),), id: 2184)
