#passage(("He says none of them wrote any Hadith Books themselves. That's a LIE! If you're talking about the Imams, you're a liar. What is the \"Muwatta of Malik\"? We have المُدَوَّنَة (alMudawwana: the Codified Record), which is by one of his students. It's a Q&A from Imam Malik. And then we have مُوَطَّأ الإمام مالِك (Muwatta of Imam Malik: the Well-Ordered Work of Imam Malik). It's a full book of Hadith of Imam Malik, and it pre-dates Bukhari.", "Right now, you're saying Bukhari came 200 years later, which is ANOTHER LIE anyway, because we have Narrations in alBukhari that are earlier than Bukhari himself. We have صَحيفَة هَمّام بن مُنَبِّه (The Sahifa: The Treatise of Hammam ibn Munabbih), who was born only 10 years after the Prophetﷺ, or so. And we have his Sahifa, written from Abu Hurayra, who was the Companion of Prophet Muhammadﷺ. So we have the Sahifa of Hammam ibn Munabbih, who was a student of Abu Hurayra, the direct Companion of Prophet Muhammadﷺ. We have it today, visible! And Imam Malik pre-dates alBukhari, and we have his Muwatta today, his full Muwatta, existing with us! So you're just a PATHETIC LIAR, saying that they haven't written anything, and saying that Bukhari comes 200 years later.", "Bukhari only compiled Narrations which already existed in previous books, like مُسنَد أحمد (Musnad: Ahmad's Hadiths collection), which also pre-dates Bukhari, by the way, or المُصنَّف لِابنِ أبي شَيبَة (alMusannaf: Ibn Abi Shaybah’s Compiled Work). All of these Books, tons of Books of Hadith that Bukhari collected his Narrations from. And he only collected the authentic Narrations. So no, Bukhari and Muslim don't come 200 years later, like you're pretending. They only collected Narrations which already existed before that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| The Quran Proves Jesus Is God?! Sunnis Don't Pray Like The Prophet?! | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbnzQHBdTJo", ((1386, "23:06–23:22"), (1405, "23:25–24:02"), (1444, "24:04–24:22"),