#passage(("Bukhari said in his own book, Tarikh Al-Bukhari تاريخ البخاري. So, I don't even need to give you isnad إسناد or anything, because Bukhari himself said it in his own book: قال البخاري في (التاريخ): وقال بعضهم عن كعب وهو أصح. يعني أن هذا الحديث مما سمعه أبو هريرة وتلقاه من كعب الأحبار، فإنهما كانا يصطحبانه ويتجالسانه للحديث، فهذا.يحدثه عن صُحفه وهذا يحدثه بما يصدّقه عن النبيﷺ فكان هذا الحديث مما تلقاه أبو هريرة عن كعب عن صُحفه، فوَهِم بعض الرواة فجعله مرفوعا إلى النبيﷺ وأكّد رفعه بقوله: أخذ رسول اللهﷺ بيدي. ثم في متنه غرابة شديدة فمن ذلك أنه ليس فيه ذكر خلق السموات، وفيه ذكر خلق الأرض وما فيها في سبعة أيام، وهذا خلاف القرآن.", "You said give me Sanad to what Al-Bukhari said. You said Sanad, and now you came and you said \"what I meant by Sanad\". It is irrelevant what you mean, because \"Sanad\" is a particular Islamic Term. No one uses except the Muslim in علم الحديث (Science of Hadith). That is a term that we invented. The term has a meaning; you cannot use a term and you say I do not mean the meaning of the term.", "What you're asking for, I already gave you, by the way. I said: قال البخاري في التاريخ. His book is Tarikh Al-Bukhari. I just gave you the exact quotation of what he said. You want the exact page? Put what I said word for word, that it will come up to you. I gave you the book and I gave you the statement word for word of what he said. It's enough for me to say Bukhari said. Even though I gave you another person quoting what Bukhari said, you said no! That's not enough, that is another person quoting Bukhari saying it. I said OK, it's the book of Al-Bukhari which is called At-Tarikh Al-Kabir, which is a very well-known book of Al-Bukhari. Open At-Tarikh Al-Kabir, go to where he talked about that Hadith and you will find it.", "Now you are a Christian. So let's see now if you apply the same methodology that you apply to that Hadith, about finding the \"Isnad\" of what is from God and what is not from God, what is correct and what is not correct. You're applying this terminology and applying this strict criteria. Let's see if you're applying the same criteria to your own book. I gave you the exact wording of what Al-Bukhari said. There's no need for me to hide from it, because it's true: he said it and he said it in his book.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Arab Christian Confronts Muslim On Bukhari! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eRixK0aX2eM", ((160, "2:40–3:04"), (246, "4:06–4:55"), (299, "4:59–5:51"), (355, "5:55–6:58"),), id: 2193)
