// U ML001:118-152 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("We say it's a hadith. Verses are in the Quran. That's number one. Number two, the hadith has explanations. [Tafsir] is a term we use for books that interpret the Quran, the [exegesis] of the Quran. There are books that interpret hadith. [Bukhari] is an example, has many books. The most prolific, most popular book that explains [Bukhari], the entirety of [Bukhari], is called [Fath al-Bari]. He says the same thing in his book. Any book explanation that you find, it says the same thing. Every book in Islamic history of scholarship that talks about this hadith says the same thing.", "We just call it explanation. Hadith we call explanation. [Tafsir], we use it specifically for the Quran. It's about terminology. I'm not telling you about explaining or not explaining. Both of them are explained. Hadith is explained by the scholars and the people of knowledge. And the Quran is explained by the scores of people of knowledge. But there are books which you call book of [tafsir]. That word is used for the Quran, for the explanation of the Quran. I'm trying to explain to you our terminologies. But you can buy a book of explanation of hadith, and I give you an example by scholars.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Agnostic Confronts A Muslim About The Treatment Of Jews In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IzncpPt4QVo", ((352, "5:52–6:38"), (409, "6:49–7:28"),), id: 2200)
// U ML246:96-117 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("This is something written by someone called Sheikh Alislam Ibn Taymiyyah, who was nearly 800 years after the Prophetﷺ. And he is one of the biggest scholars in Islamic history. This is a voluminous work called مجموعة الفتاوى (Majmu' Alfatawa: Collection of Fatwas), which is essentially a work of jurisprudence, giving verdicts on certain matters, like what is the verdict on X, Y, and Z, or not doing X, Y, and Z. This whole voluminous work is just about that, and in every other kind of matter you can think about. Even these volumes have different subjects: some will say about the prayer, some will say about this and that. So these verdicts that are recorded are about different topics.", "The scholars are not Authorities within themselves. So whatever they say, they have to use evidence from Quran or the teachings of the Prophet, to make it binding for believers to follow. If there's no evidence in the Quran or the Prophet's teachings, then it's not binding for us to follow.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Confronts Muslim On The Clarity Of The Quran! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ozeX5ELYDh0", ((319, "5:19–5:57"), (389, "6:29–6:42"),), id: 2201)

=== 36.6 The life and work of al-Albani
// NODE P06.C04.S06
#author("Farid Responds")
